.TH DT 1 "2026-07-12" "dovetail 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dt \- find, back up, and edit app configs safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dt
<\fIcommand\fR> [\fIargs\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dovetail tracks application config files, snapshots them into a git-backed
store at
.IR ~/.dotfiles ,
and pushes them back out to their live locations. Snapshots let you diff,
edit, and undo config changes safely.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B find <\fIapp\fR>
Locate an app's config (conventional paths + man page).
.TP
.B scan
Sweep
.I ~/.config
and
.I ~/
dotfiles, track what passes the guards.
.TP
.B add <\fIapp\fR> <\fIpath\fR..>
Track files/dirs manually (anything under ~).
.TP
.B untrack <\fIapp\fR>
Stop tracking an app (its history stays in the store).
.TP
.B delete <\fIapp\fR>
Snapshot, then delete an orphaned config from disk.
.TP
.B list
List tracked apps and their files.
.TP
.B backup [\fIapp\fR]
Snapshot live files into
.I ~/.dotfiles
(a git commit). If the store has a remote configured, also push.
.TP
.B push
Push the store to its remote. Does nothing if you have not configured one;
.B dt
never adds or changes the remote itself. Use a private repository.
.TP
.B apply [\fIapp\fR]
Push store copies out to the live locations.
.TP
.B diff [\fIapp\fR]
Live files vs last snapshot.
.TP
.B edit <\fIapp\fR>
Snapshot, open $EDITOR on the live files, snapshot again.
.TP
.B undo <\fIapp\fR>
Restore the previous snapshot (run again to redo).
.TP
.B open
Open the
.I ~/.dotfiles
store in Finder.
.TP
.B install\-schedule
Silent daily backup via launchd.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Override a safety refusal (backup / apply / undo).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output for
.BR list ", " diff " and " find .
See
.B JSON OUTPUT
below.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
With
.BR \-\-json ,
stdout carries exactly one JSON value and nothing else; errors stay on stderr
with a non-zero exit status.
.TP
.B dt list \-\-json
An array of
.IR "{app, paths, files}" .
Unlike the human output, an empty manifest is an empty array rather than an
error: nothing tracked is a fact, not a failure.
.TP
.B dt diff [\fIapp\fB] \-\-json
An array of
.IR "{app, file, state}" ,
where
.I state
is
.BR same ", " changed " or " never-backed-up .
This reports drift only. It does not produce a patch, because the human
.B diff
streams
.BR git-diff (1)
straight to the terminal rather than to stdout.
.TP
.B dt find \fIapp\fB \-\-json
One object:
.IR app ", " hits ", " plists ", "
.I mentions
(an array of
.IR "{path, exists}" )
and
.IR found .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dotfiles
The git-backed config store.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor launched by
.BR "dt edit" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
